<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" align="center" class="tborder" style="border-bottom: 0;">
	<tr class="titlebg">
		<td valign="middle" align="left" width="15%" style="padding-left: 6px;">
			<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/topic/normal_post.gif" alt="" />
			Author
		</td>
		<td valign="middle" align="left" width="85%" style="padding-left: 6px;">
			Topic: The Rebirth &nbsp;(Read 133 times)
		</td>
	</tr>
</table>
<table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" class="bordercolor">
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=63" title="View the profile of Mordread">Mordread</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Male.gif" alt="Male" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 37<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/spawn.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								Guardian of the Crimson Flame<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=63"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="mailto:mordread_@hotmail.com"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=122.msg378#msg378"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=122.msg378#msg378">The Rebirth</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b> on:</b> April 10, 2003, 02:29:59 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							This is my first try at a story. It's been posted on the CP page a while now. I want to write a follow up but still not gotten around to it. Hope you enjoy <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Smileys/Rodcet/smiley1.gif" alt="Smiley" border="0" /><br /><br />* * *<br /><br />The Rebirth<br /><br />The sun reflected in his red scales. He was hurt, blood mixing with his sweat. He had been fighting several dragons since he had left the safety of the dragon stronghold in the Western Wastes. His mission had brought him all over Norrath, from the wastes of Skyfire to the mountains of Butcherblock where he had finally found Dracon, close to death. His mission was to find the old Guardian of the Crimson Flame who had left the dragon halls a millennium earlier. The magical gem given to the strongest and bravest of dragons. But his secret mission had been compromised. Somehow the Ring of Scale had gotten wind of his quest and he had fought several dragons, all trying to stop him, all wanting the sacred treasure. So far he had one every battle, but not without cost. He was badly hurt and his strength was fading fast. <br /><br />The man plunged himself into the oncoming horde. From his hands came deadly shards of burning metal, ripping through the flesh of the front lines of the advancing orcs. But they kept coming. As soon as one fell another would take his place. They were determined to stop the invader, to drive him away from their lands. The man yelled out a stream of arcane words and up from the earth rose a golem, ready to do it’s masters bidding. “Pet attack!”. The orcs stared in horror for a moment but soon recovered and the onslaught continued. Wild cries of war mixed with the death screams of the ones who fell to the crushing blows of the minion and the screams of the orcs who had their flesh ripped away by burning metal. <br /><br />He had just passed over the bridge. The giants were howling below him, some even throwing huge boulders at him. He flew on without giving them more notice. His right wing was hurting badly but he was trying to ignore the pain. He was close now. As soon as he had passed the town of the giants he would be in dragon lands. He would be safe and The Flame would be safe once more. Once more be given to the strongest, the best. The fortress of the orcs was just up ahead. And it looked like there was some sort of battle going on at the moment. He flew closer, wanting to investigate the matter. Looking at the battle ahead he didn’t notice the black dragon coming from above until it was to late. The claws buried deep into his back.<br /><br />Suddenly the human stopped casting. His powers were almost gone, the frenzy had passed. With a bitter smile he shouted to the orcs to come take him. He could die now. He closed his eyes, tears running down his cheeks… His body was filled with wounds, his blonde hair smudged in blood. His own and the blood of countless orcs… he had power for one last spell. Focusing all his strength he began chanting.. the rains of magical storms of mana came down from the heavens and singed all in their path. Soon he would be engulfed by the power magics. Soon his life would end and he was filled with sadness and joy.<br /><br />The dragon screamed as the claws ripped through his scales. His chest was ripped open, the blood gushed from his death wound. He started to fall, faster and faster. He was fighting to stay conscious, wanted to at least take his enemy with him to his death. With massive effort he concentrated all his energy into one final spell. He would launch a massive ball of fire into the belly of the dragon hovering above him. As he was about to launch the spell the sky around him erupted in chaos. Magical rains were tearing his flesh. The pain was mind numbing, his spell hanging in his mind, the words not spoken but the energies ready to unleash. He crashed into the ground…<br /><br />He opened his eyes. He was not dead. How could it be. He could remember the explosion. He remembered the pain, the feeling of being torn to pieces. The feeling was still there, in his chest. But there was something else as well. He slowly lifted his hands and parted what was left of his robe. There is his chest, driven half way in, was a gem the size of a large hand. He traced it. It was strange. He did not know how it had gotten there, nor did he know how to get it out again. The world was different. He was different. In his heart, in his entire soul he felt the pain of his wounds. But they weren’t there any more. .. in the back of his mind he knew his body showed no open wounds. No scars. And there was something else… He could feel the power of the gem. And he could feel.. he closed his eyes and suddenly he was soaring high above the clouds. His mighty red wings were moving lazily, he was enjoying himself… He opened his eyes again. What was this gem. The power of it. He could feel it flowing through him. He lifted his hands and he could see the magic surrounding them. He felt so powerful and he knew the gem had something to do with it. And he knew that he must not die.. he had to carry on. And the gem was part of the reason somehow. Why he did not know.<br /><br />The lone figure walking across the icy wasteland. His tattered robe blowing in the wind. His red hair looking like flames streaming from his head. The cold did not seem to affect him. He held his head high, seeming ready to take on the world…<br />
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />Mordread Draconius<br />Arch Convoker of Cascade Point
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
</table>
